-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",95,{
[3009]="7004728D\n1\tTravel to the Hall under the Mountain, in Erebor\tThorin III is now King under the Mountain, and rules Durin's Folk from Erebor. Now that you have pledged to aid the dwarves as they adventure in Mordor, Dori believes you should meet with Thorin at the Lonely Mountain.\n2\tTalk to Foldgráf at the entrance to the Hall under the Mountain\tFoldgráf stands ready to welcome you to the Hall under the Mountain.\n3\tTalk to Bróthi in the Hall under the Mountain\030Talk to Margald in the Hall under the Mountain\030Talk to Laurík in the Hall under the Mountain\tKing Thorin is currently meeting with his advisors, and is not free for an audience. Foldgráf recommended that you make yourself familiar with the Hall under the Mountain while you wait.\n4\tFind King Thorin III, in the Hall under the Mountain\tKing Thorin should now be ready to meet with you.\n5\tTalk to Hrostyr, the personal guard of King Thorin III\tThorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor. You should present yourself to Hrostyr, his personal guard.\n6\tTalk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain\tThorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.\n7\tTalk to Eirek by the throne\030Talk to Dómor by the throne\030Talk to Mogi by the throne\tThree adventuring dwarves stand by the throne in the Hall under the Mountain. They have been charged by King Thorin III with the same task as you.\n8\tTalk to Foldgráf\tFoldgráf is at the entrance to the Hall under the Mountain.\n",
[3010]="700145B6\n1\tTalk to Thórgnyr\tThórgnyr is outside Moria by the Doors of Durin before the still pool. Slóthi wants to ensure that the supply route outside Moria remains open and that there is enough food within the mines for the dwarves to survive a long siege.\n2\tBring food supplies to Slóthi\tSlóthi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance of Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. Thórgnyr has given you the first of several food deliveries for Slóthi, who can be found in the Chamber of the Cross-roads.\n",
[3011]="7001A978\n1\tTalk to Braiglinn at Imlad Lalaith\tBraiglinn is at Imlad Lalaith on the Lothlórien side of the river Anduin. Alfirimbes is pleased that the first crossing has been successful and has sent you to Braiglinn to notify the party responsible for bringing Mazog to Dol Guldur the time has come for their own crossing.\n2\tTalk to Braiglinn and travel to meet the members of the company\tBraiglinn is at Imlad Lalaith on the Lothlórien side of the river Anduin. The time has come to meet the members of the company bringing Mazog to Dol Guldur. You should speak with Braiglinn when you are ready.\n3\tTalk to Alfirimbes at Echad Sirion\tAlfirimbes is waiting to speak with you at Echad Sirion, the camp on the shores of Anduin, on the border of Mirkwood. You have met the company responsible for bringing Mazog in secret to Dol Guldur, and they have crossed into Mirkwood. You should speak now to Alfirimbes.\n",
[3012]="700145B7\n1\tTalk to Sporr\tSporr is waiting outside the Chamber of the Cross-roads. Sigdan's cousin Sporr is to scout the approaches to the Chamber of the Cross-roads, looking for any Orcs that might be preparing to attack.\n2\tTalk to Sigdan\tSigdan is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. You have accompanied Sporr on his patrol, scouting for Orcs on the approaches to the Chamber of the Cross-roads, and should report now to Sigdan.\n",
[3013]="700145B8\n1\tFind the bottom of the well\tThe bottom of the well is likely somewhere in the Water-works, in the depths of Moria, south-west of the mighty aqueduct. The dwarf Melmar may be somewhere near the bottom. Thálfi is worried that the Orcs might climb up from the bottom of the well, and wants you to investigate to make sure that's not possible.\n2\tTalk to Thálfi\tThálfi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. You found the bottom of the well but discovered it to be well-protected, and should return now to Thálfi.\n",
[3014]="7005AC9D\n1\tBecome Hermáth Stormhammer!\tHermáth Stormhammer steps aside, allowing you to experience the Battle of Azanulbizar as he once did.\n2\tFind and rally with the Iron-folk in Amdân\tThe Iron-folk can be found in the centre of Amdân at Azanulbizar.\n3\tTalk to Dáin at Amdân\tDáin can be found among the Iron-folk at Amdân. You should talk to Dáin.\n4\tTalk to Dáin and attend the 'Council of the Seven'\tDáin can be found among the Iron-folk at Amdân. You should talk to Dáin.\n5\tTalk to Dáin at Amdân\tDáin can be found among the Iron-folk at Amdân. You should talk to Dáin.\n",
[3015]="7004729E\n1\tTalk to Prince Imrahil and return with him to the White City\tPrince Imrahil is outside the Black Gate, waiting to return with you to Minas Tirith.\n2\tTalk to King Elessar in his throne room\tKing Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.\n",
[3016]="7005A1AE\n1\tExplore the waterway\030Explore the living quarters\030Explore the balcony\030Explore the throne\030Talk to Zóva\030Talk to the Zhélruka Clan Quartermaster\030Talk to the Gundabad Missions Quartermaster\030Talk to Hórin\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes for you to explore Vérnozal.\n2\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n3\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n",
[3017]="700684E5\n1\tSpeak with Harthabor along the outer wall at Jax Phanâl\tSpeak with Harthabor at Jax Phanâl and help him obtain the response from the leader in Umbar Baharbêl. Avoid unneeded contact as you make your way to and through the outpost.\n2\tPick up a scrap of meat from the plaza near the sea-hawk\tThe sea-hawk sits atop a roof through the archway and east of Harthabor in Jax Phanâl. Find a method to draw the bird down, collect its message, and return it to the agent.\n3\tPlace the scrap of meat on the flat stone to the north-east\tThe flat stone on the rampart to the north-east should prove a suitable place to once again lure the sea-hawk from its perch.\n4\tRetrieve the latest message from the Watcher on the Wing\tYou drew the bird down from its perch and should now remove the message from its leg.\n5\tDeliver the message to Harthabor on the outer wall at Jax Phanâl\tOnce again, the bird dutifully descended from the roof-top and delivered its message. Deliver to the agent without being seen.\n6\tAttach the message to the sea-hawk courier\tThe Watcher on the Wing waits dutifully for you to bring the return message.\n7\tTalk to Harthabor\tHarthabor waits for you to return.\n",
[3018]="7006852F\n1\tSpeak with Zarai at her post in Jax Phanâl\tZarai has a concern that she needs to address. Speak with her in Jax Phanâl.\n2\tFind the satchel along the foot of the mountains to the south-east\tZarai provided a general area east along the mountains where a courier lost their delivery. She requires that the satchel reaches Aphamâr, the ledger-keeper of Rakhatâb.\n3\tDeliver the runed leather satchel to Aphamâr in Rakhatâb\tWith the satchel recovered you should deliver it to the ledger-keeper Aphamâr in Rakhatâb. You were told she usually stands across the path from the stable-master.\n4\tAphamâr is not where you expected to find her. Núrut of Rakhatâb likely knows her whereabouts. Find and speak with the dwarf near their office at the crest of Rakhatâb.\t\n5\tDeliver the runed satchel to Aphamâr at Rahâl Ghol in Umbar Baharbêl\tFind Aphamâr in Râhal Ghol, the upper ward of Umbar Bahârbel.\n",
[3019]="70064BE8\n1\tTalk to Caebar by the eastern entrance of Linhir, in King's Gondor\tCaebar is by the eastern entrance of the town of Linhir, in King's Gondor.\n2\tDefeat pests in Linhir (total: 6)\030Hear the concerns of Nimdol\030Hear the concerns of Maeriel\030Hear the concerns of Forcharn\tCaebar made a list of the most common complaints of Linhir's townsfolk: foes in Dor-en-Ernil, pests in the town, burned timbers in Linhir, and listening to the concerns of the people.\n3\tTalk to Caebar by the eastern entrance of Linhir, in King's Gondor\tCaebar is by the eastern entrance of the town of Linhir, in King's Gondor.\n4\tTravel to Barad Rill, the grand lighthouse in Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor\tBarad Rill is located to the south-west of Linhir, at the southern point of the peninsula of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.\n5\tTalk to Caebar in view of Barad Rill, in King's Gondor\tCaebar stares at the ruin of Barad Rill at the southern peninsula of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.\n6\tExamine the sketch of Barad Rill given to you by Caebar\tCaebar gave you a sketch of the lighthouse of Barad Rill, seen in happier days.\n7\tReturn Caebar's sketch of Barad Rill to him\tCaebar stares at the ruin of Barad Rill at the southern peninsula of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.\n8\tDefeat enemies of Gondor in Dor-en-Ernil or the Ringló Vale, King's Gondor (total: 10)\tCaebar has a renewed interest in facing the foes of Gondor that prowl Dor-en-Ernil or the Ringló Vale, in King's Gondor.\n9\tTravel to the southern entrance of Ethring, in the Ringló Vale, King's Gondor\tCaebar's hometown of Ethring is located in the Ringló Vale, north of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.\n10\tTalk to Uilin at the entrance of Ethring, in King's Gondor\tUilin stands at the entrance of Ethring, glaring at you and Caebar.\n",
[3020]="70064BE7\n1\tTalk to Caebar at the entrance of Ethring\tCaebar has returned home to Ethring, but it is not a pleasant homecoming.\n2\tFind the home of Caebar's mother, Sirdis\tCaebar's mother's house is to the north across the bridge and to the right, in the village of Ethring, in King's Gondor.\n3\tTalk to Carlong in front of Sirdis's house\tCarlong blocks the way into the home of Caebar's mother, Sirdis.\n4\tTalk to Caebar outside his mother's house in Ethring, in King's Gondor\tCaebar stands outside his mother's house in Ethring, in King's Gondor.\n5\tCaebar wants you to listen to the concerns of Ethring's villagers.\t\n6\tTalk to Caebar outside his mother's house in Ethring, in King's Gondor\tCaebar stands outside his mother's house in Ethring, in King's Gondor.\n7\tTravel to the entrance of Calembel in Lamedon, King's Gondor\tThe town of Calembel is north-west of the Ringló Vale, in Lamedon, King's Gondor.\n8\tTalk to Garthaben south of Calembel, in King's Gondor\tGarthaben calls excitedly to you south-east of the entrance to Calembel.\n9\tEnter Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts in the south-west corner of Calembel, in King's Gondor\tGalengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts is in the south-west corner of Calembel, in King's Gondor.\n10\tTalk to Galengam inside his shop in Calembel, King's Gondor\tGalengam is inside his crowded shop in the south-west corner of Calembel, in King's Gondor.\n",
[3021]="70064BEC\n1\tTalk to Queen Arwen in Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts\tQueen Arwen is inside Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, in Calembel, King's Gondor.\n2\tTalk to King Elessar in Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts\tKing Elessar is inside Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, in Calembel, King's Gondor.\n3\tTravel to the western entrance south of Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor\tRossaran will meet you and the rest of the company at the western entrance south of Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor.\n4\tTalk to Rossaran at the western entrance south of Dol Amroth and travel with him to see Prince Imrahil\tThe Swan-knight Rossaran stands at the western entrance south of Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor, waiting to bring you to Prince Imrahil.\n5\tTalk to Prince Imrahil in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor\tPrince Imrahil is inside the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor.\n",
[3022]="70064BB6\n1\tTalk to King Elessar in the Imloth Melui guard-house\tKing Elessar is inside the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor.\n2\tEnter the Hall of Lady Vanyalos in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor\tThe Hall of Lady Vanyalos is to the east of the tower guard-house in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.\n3\tTalk to Ioreth in the Hall of Lady Vanyalos\tThe Hall of Lady Vanyalos is to the east of the tower guard-house in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.\n4\tTalk to Lady Vanyalos in her hall\tThe Hall of Lady Vanyalos is to the east of the tower guard-house in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.\n5\tTalk to Queen Arwen in the Hall of Lady Vanyalos\tThe Hall of Lady Vanyalos is to the east of the tower guard-house in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.\n6\tFill the bowl with water from the falls in the north-western reaches of Imloth Melui\030Fill the bowl with water from a fountain outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos\tArwen asked you to fill the ceramic bowl she gave you with water from one of the fountains outside the Hall of Lady Vanyalos and with water from one of the falls in the north-western reaches of Imloth Melui.\n7\tReturn the ceramic bowl filled with water to Queen Arwen in the Hall of Lady Vanyalos, in King's Gondor\tQueen Arwen is in the Hall of Lady Vanyalos, in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.\n8\tTalk to Lady Vanyalos in her hall, in King's Gondor\tLady Vanyalos is in her hall in Imloth Melui, King's Gondor.\n9\tTalk to King Elessar in the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor\tKing Elessar is in the tower guard-house in the centre of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor.\n",
[3023]="70047CEC\n1\tTalk to Frideric the Elder in Ost Guruth\tFrideric the Elder is in Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands. Mithrandir believes the Eglain of the Lone-lands may know something about the corrupted heirloom of Cardolan you discovered.\n2\tTalk to Cythred on Weathertop\tCythred is on the hill of Weathertop, in the Lone-lands.\n3\tTalk to Séca on Weathertop\tSéca is on Weathertop. You have defended Cythred from an attack, and now his assistant Séca wishes to thank you.\n4\tFind the Scholar's Stair Archives in Bree-town\tSéca of the Eglain told you to consult with Newbold Leafcutter in the Scholar's Stair Archives in the Town of Bree.\n5\tTalk to Newbold Leafcutter in the Scholar's Stair Archive\tNewbold Leafcutter is in the Scholar's Stair Archive in the Town of Bree.\n6\tDefeat evil-fascinated wights outside Haudh Nogbenn ([see journal]/3)\tHaudh Nogbenn is at the southern tip of the Northern Barrow-downs. Newbold Leafcutter thinks that evils will be drawn to the sceptre when you bring it to Haudh Nogbenn.\n7\tDefeat evil-fascinated wights outside Haudh Nogbenn (2/3)\tHaudh Nogbenn is at the southern tip of the Northern Barrow-downs. Newbold Leafcutter thinks that evils will be drawn to the sceptre when you bring it to Haudh Nogbenn.\n8\tExamine the wooden shield and search Haudh Nogbenn for its owner\tA fallen wooden shield catches your eye outside the entrance to the barrow of Haudh Nogbenn.\n9\tBring the Sceptre of Cardolan to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House. You have cleansed the corruption from the Sceptre of Cardolan, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.\n",
[3024]="70047CF6\n1\tTalk to Greith in the Twenty-first Hall, in Khazad-dûm\tGreith in the Twenty-first Hall considers himself a master of locks and keys and is always telling people so. Mithrandir thinks that finding the door unlocked by the corrupted key might cleanse the heirloom of its evil.\n2\tUnlock the door south-west of the Twenty-first Hall with the Corrupted Key\tGreith told you of a number of doors south-west of the Twenty-first Hall that the corrupted key might unlock.\n3\tUnlock the door south-west of the Twenty-first Hall with the Corrupted Key\tGreith told you of a number of doors south-west of the Twenty-first Hall that the corrupted key might unlock.\n4\tTalk to Greith outside the unlocked door south-west of the Twenty-first Hall and down many levels\tGreith is outside the unlocked door in Khazad-dûm, south-west of the Twenty-first Hall and down many levels.\n5\tTalk to Greith outside the unlocked door and explore beyond\tGreith is outside the unlocked door south-west of the Twenty-first Hall and down many levels, in Khazad-dûm.\n6\tBring the Key of the Forgotten to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House. You have cleansed the corruption from the Key of the Forgotten, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.\n",
[3025]="70066952\n1\tFind a sailor in Osgiliath who knows about the corrupted rigging-hook\tMithrandir believes you should ask sailors in Osgiliath if they know the story of the rigging-hook you found in Mordor. Now that soldiers of the Host of the West have passed through Osgiliath, the city should be reasonably safe for you to search for such a sailor.\n2\tTalk to Nathlad in Osgiliath and learn what he knows of the corrupted rigging-hook\tNathlad in Osgiliath is waiting for to agree to help him with his work before he tells you what he knows of the rigging-hook you recovered from Mordor.\n3\tBring the Anchor of the Past to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House. You have cleansed the corruption from the Anchor of the Past, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.\n",
[3026]="70047CED\n1\tTalk to Elrond in his library in Rivendell\tElrond can be found in the library of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell.\n2\tThe course of the Bruinen in the Misty Mountains falls in three levels before it comes out of the mountains. Elrond asked you to fill the cup of Rhudaur with cold, clear water from waterfalls in the Misty Mountains, and to defeat any creatures drawn by its corruption.\t\n3\tTalk to Elrond in the library of Rivendell\tElrond is in the library of Rivendell.\n4\tTalk to Elrond and travel to the Lost Temple to cleanse the Cup of Rhudaur\tElrond is in his library in Rivendell, waiting to advise you about your journey to the Lost Temple to cleanse the cup of Rhudaur.\n5\tBring the Cup of Sacrifice to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House. You have cleansed the corruption from the Cup of Sacrifice and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.\n",
[3027]="70047D18\n1\tTalk to Chief Tuokki at Lehmä-koti\tChief Tuokki is at the Earth-kin village of Lehmä-koti, in the Ram Dúath, south of Angmar.\n2\tTalk to Aarnikka in Lehmä-koti\030Talk to Santtu in Lehmä-koti\tAarnikka and Santtu can be found in the village of Lehmä-koti and may know something about the corrupted pouch.\n3\tFind the pond revered by the Rauta-lehmä near Kar Lak, in Nan Amlug East\tThere is a pond in the North Downs, in the south-east corner of Nan Amlug East, where the Rauta-lehmä gather. Santtu told you Trotsiv was going to go there, but he is worried that something happened to him because the pond is very near to Kar Lak, war-camp of the Rauta-lehmä.\n4\tDefeat evil-fascinated Wargs at the pond near Kar Lak ([see journal]/3)\tA pack of hunting Wargs has been drawn to you by the evil emanating from the corrupted pouch.\n5\tDefeat evil-fascinated Wargs at the pond near Kar Lak (2/3)\tA pack of hunting Wargs has been drawn to you by the evil emanating from the corrupted pouch.\n6\tTalk to Rhothlas by the pond near Kar Lak\tYou have found an Ent near a pond in the North Downs.\n7\tTalk to Rhothlas and hear his tale\tRhothlas is standing among the trees near the pond in Nan Amlug East, below Kar Lak.\n8\tBring the Seeds of Defiance to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House. You have cleansed the corruption from the Seeds of Defiance, and should bring them now to Elrond in Rivendell.\n",
[3028]="70047CE4\n1\tTalk to Frideric the Elder in Ost Guruth\tFrideric the Elder is in Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands. Mithrandir believes that the corrupted heirloom you have recovered has some connexion to the Eglain of the Lone-lands.\n2\tTalk to Morhald in Haragmar\030Talk to Cólbyr in Haragmar\tMorhald and Cólbyr search the Haragmar east of Ost Guruth for artifacts such as the one that has come into your possession.\n3\tTalk to Walgar in Haragmar\tMore of the Eglain may be imperiled in the swamp of Haragmar.\n4\tTalk to Aric the Stone-speaker in Harloeg\tAric the Stone-speaker is at Ost Haer, far to the south of Haragmar.\n5\tTalk to Aric the Stone-speaker and travel to the Spring of the Red-maid\tAric the Stone-speaker is in Harloeg, far south of Ost Guruth.\n6\tBring the Image of the Champion to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House. You have cleansed the corruption from the Image of the Champion, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.\n",
[3029]="70047CF3\n1\tTalk to Techeron at Echad Garthadir, in Annúminas\tTecheron returned to Echad Garthadir in Annúminas following the War of the Ring. Mithrandir believes that the corrupted badge came at first from Annúminas in the days of High King Elendil.\n2\tTalk to Línneth in Annúminas\030Talk to Carastír in Annúminas\tTecheron sent you to find the Steadfast Sisters in Annúminas, to see if they have seen any badges identical to the one that came out of Mordor.\n3\tTalk to Gwíniel in Annúminas\tGwíniel is near the gate of Adannon, in Annúminas.\n4\tTalk to Colm Fettering on Rantost\tColm Fettering is a tomb-robber of some notoriety on the island of Rantost, in Lake Evendim, and may tell you more about the corrupted badge.\n5\tTalk to Techeron at Echad Garthadir, in Annúminas\tTecheron is at Echad Garthadir, in Annúminas.\n6\tTalk to Techeron and walk with him to the Bridge of Ariant\tTecheron is at Echad Garthadir, in Annúminas.\n7\tBring the Badge of Ariant to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House. You have cleansed the corruption from the Badge of Ariant, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.\n",
[3030]="70058699\n1\tTalk to Anlaf the Forlorn in the Forsaken Inn\tAnlaf the Forlorn tends the bar of the Forsaken Inn, in the Lone-lands.\n2\tBring the corrupted necklace to Umín somewhere outside the Forsaken Inn\tAnlaf told you that Umín just left the Forsaken Inn, and if you hurry you might see him outside somewhere.\n3\tTalk to Umín and return to the ship in the caverns beneath the Forsaken Inn\tUmín has struggled greatly since his encounter with the spirit of the necklace in the caverns beneath the Forsaken Inn.\n4\tBring the Necklace of the Ordinary to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House. You have cleansed the corruption from the Necklace of the Ordinary, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.\n",
[3031]="70047D4F\n1\tTalk to the expert jeweller in Minas Tirith, on the southern side of the Fourth Circle, after the battle\tAn expert jeweller in Minas Tirith may be able to use his tools to read the markings on the corrupted shard for you. Such a jeweller plies his trade on the southern side of the Fourth Circle, after the battle.\n2\tTalk to the expert jeweller in Snowbourn\tOne jeweller sent you to another. Perhaps the expert jeweller in Snowbourn, the city of Rohan in the Sutcrofts, will be able to read the markings on the corrupted tusk-shard.\n3\tTalk to the bard in the tavern in Aldburg\tThe jeweller in Snowbourn sent you to the village of Aldburg, in the Eastfold, to ask a Bard of Rohan about the tusk-shard.\n4\tTalk to Eldmath north-east of Aldburg\tEldmath has gone ahead into the field, inspired by the promise of adventure and planned to meet you north-east of Aldburg.\n5\tDefeat Wargs drawn by the corruption (total: 2)\tYou should defeat the Wargs drawn by the corruption of the tusk-shard, or they might prove a danger to Eldmath or the people of the Eastfold.\n6\tCatch up with Eldmath\tEldmath ran off during the fighting, and you should find him. He cannot have gone far.\n7\tTalk to Tharbag and look for an opportunity to rescue Eldmath\tEldmath has been captured by a raiding party of Orcs.\n8\tBring the Vengeance of Folca to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House. You have cleansed the corruption from the Vengeance of Folca and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.\n",
[3032]="70047CF4\n1\tTalk to Lothrandir in Sûri-kylä, in Forochel\tLothrandir returned to Sûri-kylä in Forochel following the War of the Ring. Mithrandir believes that the corrupted brooch came from Forochel and returning it there may help cleanse the corruption that befell it in Mordor.\n2\tSearch for the missing Lossoth warriors east of Sûri-kylä\tLothrandir asked you to search east of Sûri-kylä while he showed the corrupted brooch to folk in the city.\n3\tTalk to Terho\tTerho is south-east of Sûri-kylä, calling for help!\n4\tTalk to Lothrandir in Sûri-kylä, in Forochel\tLothrandir returned to Sûri-kylä in Forochel following the War of the Ring.\n5\tTalk to Lothrandir in Sûri-kylä and go to see the widow\tLothrandir returned to Sûri-kylä in Forochel following the War of the Ring. Lothrandir gave the corrupted brooch to its rightful owner, but he fears that if the corruption remains it might do her some harm.\n6\tBring the Brooch of Bone to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House. You have cleansed the corruption from the Brooch of Bone, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.\n",
[3033]="70047CF8\n1\tTalk to Suvulch in the village of Lhanuch\tSuvulch is in the village of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith.\n2\tTalk to Helû in Lhanuch\tHelû is a warrior of Lhanuch on the highest rise of the village.\n3\tTalk to Lhunog on a hill outside Lhanuch\tLhunog is on a hill outside the village of Lhanuch.\n4\tTalk to Helû outside the village\tHelû has come out of the village for further investigation of the bone fragment.\n5\tTalk to Hûdh of the Caru-lûth in Galtrev\030Talk to Cufrus of the Avanc-lûth, in Galtrev\tHûdh of the Caru-lûth and Cufrus of the Avanc-lûth are in Galtrev and may know more of the bone fragment you carry.\n6\tTalk to Frestang of the Uch-lûth, in Galtrev\tFrestang of the Uch-lûth is in Galtrev.\n7\tTalk to the expert tailor in the Hall of Making, in Lhanuch\tAn expert tailor in the Hall of Making in Lhanuch may know something about the needle that came into your possession.\n8\tTalk to Raiglud in the Hall of Making, in Lhanuch\tRaiglud, the oldest woman in Lhanuch, has drawn your attention. She is in the Hall of Making, and has a story to tell.\n9\tTalk to Raiglud and listen to her tale of long ago\tRaiglud, the oldest woman in Lhanuch, has drawn your attention. She is in the Hall of Making, and has a story to tell.\n10\tBring the Needle of Many Leagues to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House. You have cleansed the corruption from the Needle of Many Leagues, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.\n",
[3034]="70047D4E\n1\tTalk to Ghân-buri-Ghân at Drû Bhûta\tGhân-buri-Ghân is the leader of the Drúedain and may know the origins of the corrupted carving. He is at Drû Bhûta, in Taur Drúadan.\n2\tTalk to Khôr-buri-Ghân at the Blood-cloak, in Drû Bhûta\tKhôr-buri-Ghân is at the Blood-cloak, east of the great waterfall in Drû Bhûta, atop a large rocky cliff. It is the location where the Wild Men perform their funerary rites.\n3\tLook for Orcs north of the road by Drû Bhûta, in Taur Drúadan\030Look for Orcs further north-east in the woods, in Taur Drúadan\tKhôr-buri-Ghân suggested that you look for Orcs at two places in Taur Drúadan, forth of Drû Bhûta and further north-east of there, in the woods.\n4\tLook for Orcs to the north-west, over a hill and by an island in the river, in Taur Drúadan\tKhôr-buri-Ghân suggested that you look for Orcs at another place in Taur Drúadan, north-west over a hill.\n5\tTalk to Khôr-buri-Ghân by the river and travel with him to the island cave\tKhôr-buri-Ghân has remembered a cave that his brother told him about and wants to find it. He is by the island in the river, waiting for you to speak with him.\n6\tBring the Memento of Bhai-buri-Ghân to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is at the Haven of Orladion in Rivendell, north-west of the Last Homely House. You have cleansed the corruption from the Memento of Bhai-buri-Ghân, and should bring it now to Elrond in Rivendell.\n",
[3035]="70056F60\n1\tTalk to Imák at the entrance of the pass to Misthallow\030Talk to Venko at the entrance of the pass to Misthallow\tImák and Venko are at the entrance to the pass that leads to Misthallow, east and south of the broken Rushgate.\n2\tCross into Misthallow, the northern reaches of the Wells of Langflood\tIt is time for you and your travelling companions to cross into Misthallow, the foggy basin in the northern reaches of the Wells of Langflood.\n3\tDefeat beasts or other dangers in Misthallow (total: 8)\030Explore potential camp-site location east of Hlithseld\030Explore potential camp-site location south-east of Hlithseld\tIn order to find a safe camp-site, you will need to slay aggressive beasts in Misthallow and scout for possible places to shelter out of the wind.\n4\tExplore potential camp-site location beside the rocks south-east of Hlithseld\tImák has pointed out a spot that might make for a suitable camp-site.\n5\tTalk to Glóin\tYour travelling companions have found a suitable camp-site south-east of Hlithseld in Misthallow.\n",
[3036]="70056F71\n1\tHelp Venko with 'Promises Unkept'\030Help Imák with 'A Nose for Danger'\tImák and Venko need your help setting up the camp-site.\n2\tTalk to Glóin at your camp-site in Misthallow\tGlóin is at your camp-site in Misthallow.\n",
[3037]="70048C40\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir outside the Black Gate\tMithrandir is outside the Black Gate.\n",
[3038]="70064BB7\n1\tTravel to the main square of Arnach, south of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor\tThe town of Arnach is located to the south of Imloth Melui, in King's Gondor.\n2\tFolk of Arnach gather in the main square of the village, staring at the King and his party.\t\n3\tTalk to Elessar in the main square of Arnach\tKing Elessar is in the main square of the village of Arnach.\n4\tPick berries from bushes to the south-east of Arnach (total: 4)\tBerry bushes can be found to the south-east of Arnach, in King's Gondor.\n5\tTalk to Elladan south-east of Arnach, in King's Gondor\tElladan stands picking berries to the south-east of Arnach, in King's Gondor.\n6\tPrepare meat of the slain deer to the south-east of Elladan\tElladan asked you to begin preparing the meat of the slain deer just to the south-east.\n7\tTalk to Queen Arwen south-east of Arnach, in King's Gondor\tQueen Arwen is hunting south-east of Arnach.\n8\tBring Elrohir's bow and quiver to him in Arnach, King's Gondor\tElrohir is working alongside King Elessar in the village of Arnach, in King's Gondor.\n9\tTalk to King Elessar in Arnach, King's Gondor\tKing Elessar is working in the village of Arnach, in King's Gondor.\n10\tTalk to Baranor in the centre of Arnach, in King's Gondor\tBaranor is in the centre of Arnach, in King's Gondor.\n11\tTalk to King Elessar in Arnach, King's Gondor\tKing Elessar is working in the village of Arnach, in King's Gondor.\n",
[3039]="70056FAB\n1\tTalk to Venko at your camp-site in Misthallow\030Talk to Imák at your camp-site in Misthallow\tImák and Venko are at your camp-site in Misthallow, and they have some thoughts about Glóin's tale.\n2\tTalk to Glóin at your camp-site in Misthallow\tGlóin is at your camp-site in Misthallow.\n3\tEat in silence, leaving your companions to their thoughts\030Drink in silence, leaving your companions to their thoughts\tSilence has fallen upon your camp-site, and your companions eat and drink in silence.\n4\tTalk to Glóin at your camp-site in Misthallow\tGlóin is at your camp-site in Misthallow.\n",
[3040]="70064BDD\n1\tTalk to Captain Imladir in the centre of Tumladen, in King's Gondor\tCaptain Imladir is in the centre of the refuge of Tumladen, located to the west of Arnach, in King's Gondor.\n2\tFind the dwarves from Furukzahar to the south-east of Captain Imladir, in Tumladen\tImladir asked you to find the dwarves from Furukzahar where he saw them last, to the south-east.\n3\tBow to the dwarf-expedition from Furukzahar\tThe dwarves from Furukzahar stand in Tumladen, waiting for a friendly bow of greeting.\n4\tTalk to Asitám in Tumladen, King's Gondor\tAn expedition of dwarves has come from Furukzahar with a proposal for the people of Tumladen.\n5\tSurvey debris within Tumladen up the slope to the north-east\tThe dwarves from Furukzahar intend to survey the debris within Tumladen, up the slope to the north-east.\n6\tSurvey debris within Tumladen further up the slope to the north-west\tThe dwarves from Furukzahar intend to survey the debris within Tumladen, further up the slope to the north-west.\n7\tSurvey debris deeper within Tumladen to the north-east\tThe dwarves from Furukzahar intend to survey the debris deeper within Tumladen to the north-east.\n8\tSurvey debris deeper within Tumladen to the north-east\tA nearby resident of Tumladen stares at the dwarves with anger in his eyes.\n9\tKing Elessar would not appreciate any violence between the Dwarves of Furukzahar and the residents of Tumladen.\t\n10\tTalk to Asitám in Tumladen\tYou have prevented violence between the dwarves from Furukzahar and residents of Tumladen, and should now speak to Asitám.\n11\tTalk to Captain Imladir in Tumladen, King's Gondor\tCaptain Imladir is in the centre of Tumladen, in King's Gondor.\n12\tTalk to King Elessar on the eastern docks of Pelargir, in King's Gondor\tKing Elessar stands by the eastern docks of Pelargir, in King's Gondor.\n",
})
